      "id": "FWF-01",
      "chapter": "global",
      "title": "A fixed witness admits a bounded set of isotropic graph lifts",
      "anchor": "global-fixed-witness-flags",
      "statement": "A fixed P contained in the definite row lattice with rank k−s and determinant at most Δ contributes at most (N²Δ)^r choices of graph lift modulo the frame-fixing integral unipotents, after passing to exact Gram data in a split row. All contributing flag classes are covered by the fixed-lift sets.",
      "hypotheses": "N=T(u)^f, r is the isotropic rank, 1≤s≤k, Δ≥1. For the uniform caller use its full standing and numerical Hyp on the two words, Cℓ≥1, a standard base flag, an admissible row and a relevant Gram cell. The good Gram data for an occupied flag set use Q=HHZ(Z)². The arithmetic sublattice is required to be contained in the visible lattice.",
