      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "The integral definite saturation has determinant at least one. Its index over P is at most Δ by the determinant-index identity. For an occupied relevant class the chosen bounded Gram representative is Z itself. Transport a class to its exact representative in a split row. On each of r coordinates, restriction from the primitive saturation costs at most its index and linear forms modulo pairings from the row cost at most N². Represent the differences by actual integral unipotent moves. Cover the exact classes by the resulting finitely many graphs without assuming their fibres are disjoint.",
      "review": "Checked the sublattice inclusion direction, the field rank after taking spans, the saturation index, the witness Z₁=Z, and the precise two-part count on linear forms."
    },
