      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "For the top r-by-(r+1) matrix Y of the exact Gram, the cofactor combination y of the dual-lattice components obeys T(u)h(y,y)=G. Positivity and the denominator ideal make the product of the embedded squared lengths of any nonzero difference at least 1/N(I). Packing bounds the choices for y by 9^{sf}(MQ)^s. Subtracting a representative for y kills the cofactor. The adjugate then gives r row coefficients modulo S₀ with at most (MQ)^{sr} choices. Eichler moves effect the row shifts. At fixed components the frame difference solves x*Y+Y*x=0 and integral central maps add cY with c skew-Hermitian. The minor and denominator ideal bound the remaining classes. The classes are contained in the image of the finite product.",
      "review": "For Y=(t,0) over the Gaussian integers, S₀ self-dual of rank one and |tw₁|²=t², direct orbit enumeration gives 4t² perpendicular and t skew classes for t=1,2,3. At t=2 the two coordinate sets give 32 ordered pairs. The model only tests these two coordinate equations and quotient relations."
    },
