  "outstanding": [
    "The argument uses the common-frame arithmetic hypotheses, the existence of a split row under an isometry fixing the base frame, the realization of exact Gram frames, the bound for primitive linear forms modulo lattice pairings, and the perpendicular-ideal and frame-geometry lemmas. The subsequent count and genus average of primitive witness sublattices are separate from the fixed-witness bound."
